+- Validation: `node scripts/validate-paragraph.js --mode part-a "<paragraph-folder>"` PASS (exit 0) after final independent review and explicit migration of the legacy Part A-only quality record to schema 2. `paragraph-records.js quality` successfully derived the current record (exit 0). No companion block existed or was changed.
+- No remote PR, push, CI execution, publication, deployment or merge: local-only assessment instruction.
+
+## 2. Textbook Source Files
+
+`2.1.1 Kostenstructuren – paragraaf.md`, `– opgaven.md`, `– antwoorden.md`, with matching HTML and PDF files. The final packet has 11 paragraph pages, 8 exercise pages and 6 answer pages. `build_pdf.py` is the thin shared-renderer wrapper. ZIP packaging is optional and outside the required paragraph output contract. The refreshed exercise ZIP is preserved as external delivery evidence at `C:/wt/reorganize 2/authoring-assessment-20260913/paragraph/closure-20260914/delivery/2.1.1 Kostenstructuren – opgaven.zip`, with its hash and member checks in `closure-20260914/packaging-verify.json`. The tracked legacy ZIP was restored to lesson baseline `0acaaa97443e5c4fee34f7da8a12ccd5db62d762`; it is not the delivery package for this draft.
+
+Publisher-print chapter/book assembly is outside this assignment. All page renders and executable geometry checks are preserved outside the repository in the assessment run folder (`qa-pages-repair-v2`, preserved `qa-pages-final`, `changed-pages.json`, `figure-geometry.json`, `source-output-checks.json`, `html-check.json`). The independent report states its own coverage. Local HTML browser navigation returned `net::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT`; browser-specific visual behaviour is unverified. Saved HTML has passed static structure/asset checks. Any independent offline screen-media rendering coverage is recorded by the reviewer.
+
+## 3. Target Exercise And Operation Chain
+
+Exact approved registry target: Bakkerij De Korenaar, hash `143f1053c98766b77d9d9ce573a5c8e976980f900387159312c3238288d71710`. Source/action authority is `2.1.1-textbook-foundation.json`; Part A action `paragraph_production` passed. Do not infer a new source approval from this handoff.
+
+Target operations: classify four cost components with reasons; build TCK=500, TVK=0.80Q, TK=500+0.80Q; calculate GCK/GVK/GTK at Q=500 and 1,000; compare every total and explain each average within one month and unchanged capacity. Target points 4/3/3/3/4. Answer forms: classification table, three functions, two cost rows with full units, bounded causal explanation. No graph drawing is required.
+
+Skills A08, A14, A50, A86, D38 are the record's target labels. Only A04 substitution/endpoint checks and actually taught table/graph reading are retrieved. Cost classification and euro/period versus euro/product are formal new learning here. D02 profit/MO=MK is not inherited.
+
+## 4. Concepts And Terminology
+
+| Concept | Meaning | Formula and condition | Avoid |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Constante kosten | Total does not change with Q within period/capacity | TCK is sum of fixed period amounts | Classifying by invoice name or frequency |
+| Variabele kosten | Total changes with Q | TVK=vQ only when v is constant per product | Saying variable always means changing per product |
+| Totale kosten | Entire production in one period | TK=TCK+TVK | Dropping the time-period unit |
+| Gemiddelde kosten | Relevant total divided over products | GCK=TCK/Q; GVK=TVK/Q; GTK=TK/Q=GCK+GVK, Q>0 | Treating TCK as fixed cost per product |
+
+## 5. Procedures
+
+Use the worked example's sequence: (1) classify each component by total behaviour; (2) sum fixed amounts and unit variable amounts, then construct functions; (3) substitute Q, find totals and divide each by Q with units; (4) compare totals first and averages second, explain causes and limits. Answers use this same chain. The plan maps the approved operation IDs and goals; no new registry operation is minted.
+
+## 6. Core Visuals
+
+| Asset pair | Purpose | Reuse boundary |
+|---|---|---|
+| `_assets/2.1.1_fig_1.svg` and `.png` | Totals → divide by Q → averages; addition across rows | Keep Q>0 and both unit levels visible. |
+| `_assets/2.1.1_fig_2.svg` and `.png` | TCK/TVK/TK for keychain atelier | Q=100–200 per week; TCK=120, TVK=.50Q, TK=120+.50Q euro/week. |
+| `_assets/2.1.1_fig_3.svg` and `.png` | GCK/GVK/GTK for same model | Same Q domain; per-keychain units; constant GVK is conditional. |
+
+The six numerical curves have 606 equation-checked saved SVG vertices. Endpoint labels use explicit leader lines where averages approach each other. Preserve direct labels and patterns so colour is not the sole distinction.
+
+## 7. Exercise Map
+
+| Exercise | Operation | Answer location | Scaffolding |
