+# Part A Textbook Plan: 2.1.1 Kostenstructuren
+
+New complete draft for 4vwo, 13 September 2026. Author: assessment-paragraph.
+
+## Book foundation check
+
+[Book foundation check](2.1.1-textbook-foundation.json) binds the approved outline, current registry, exact target and scoped holds. Generated at platform 85b0f347f3070e005eae3f35f0b11ce6eac71b4d with `paragraph-records.js foundation ... --action paragraph_production`.
+
+Current action: `paragraph_production`. Foundation verdict: `PASS_FOR_PARAGRAPH_PRODUCTION`. The generated action check passed; applicable target and outline holds are released. Historical draft labels do not supersede validated lifecycle state. This grants no publication or merge authority.
+
+Local chapter authority: `../_chapter-plan.md` at lesson 0acaaa97443e5c4fee34f7da8a12ccd5db62d762 retains the four-paragraph order and theory/consolidation distinction. Its hash matches the foundation audit pin. Use that structural placement for this expressly assigned fresh paragraph draft. Its historical reviewed-final target narrative is not used as current target approval; current exact registry and action authority come from the generated foundation. No chapter assembly or chapter approval is claimed.
+
+### Canonical paragraph semantics
+
+Role: establish behaviour-based constant/variable classification, TCK/TVK/TK functions, GCK/GVK/GTK calculation, total-versus-average interpretation, and causal comparison at two quantities. Canonical semantics: platform `references/authored/book-outlines/book-2-outline.md`, §2.1 paragraph row and entry prerequisites.
+
+| Incoming operation | Classification | Evidence and support decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| Read columns, units and two rows from a table | previously_taught_retrieval_required | Actual §1.1.3 textbook lines 21–30 teach this procedure. Opgave 1 retrieves it; no claim that every learner is secure. |
+| Read axis labels and follow a supplied curve | previously_taught_retrieval_required | Actual §1.1.3 lines 78–100; briefly recalled before the first cost graph. Graphs support understanding, never add a terminal drawing task. |
+| Substitute and check endpoint units | previously_taught_retrieval_required | Registry explicitly permits A04 only; simple numerical substitution is shown in the worked example and accessible guided route. |
+| Formal cost classification, euro/period versus euro/product, functions and averages | new_formal_learning | Registry goals 1–4 and prior-knowledge boundary; taught fully here. |
+| Book 1 supplied cost/profit formulas | preview_or_familiarity_only | Owned pedagogical boundaries lines 123–128; no shortening of formal teaching. |
+
+No operation is classified probably secure without learner evidence. No extra operation is assumed not-secure: the printed guided route supplies help when retrieval reveals a gap. The five-category framework is applied per operation, not as a requirement to populate all categories.
+
+Non-goals: revenue, profit, break-even, marginal costs, MO=MK, formal proportional/degressive/progressive classification, graph production. D38's D02 profit prerequisite is explicitly not inherited, following the approved target record. Prepares for §§2.1.2–2.1.4 and the supply-as-MC bridge in §2.3.2, without teaching those operations now.
+
+Models always name one period, unchanged capacity and a bounded Q range. Average formulas require Q>0. Constant GVK follows only from constant variable cost per product. A second scenario may change the fixed contract and the unit input price; the new scenario is identified explicitly, not described as ceteris paribus.
+
+## Part A backward-design plan
+
+### Goals and target route
+
+Target: exact registry `2.1.1`, Bakkerij De Korenaar, target hash `143f1053c98766b77d9d9ce573a5c8e976980f900387159312c3238288d71710`. Preserve context, table, a–e wording and 4/3/3/3/4 point allocation. This is an owned blueprint target, not an official CvTE question; no official annex or correction model is claimed. Source route is owned blueprint → current target record → unchanged capstone. Internal syllabus mapping: D1.16, D1.17, A2.10; operations A08, A14, A50, A86, D38 per record.
+
+| Goal | Target operation | Worked example | Start check | Guided | Independent | Coverage |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Classify by output behaviour | a: classify each component and explain change in total | Keychain atelier step 1, four components | 2a–b | 3a | 4a, 5a | Covered |
+| Formulate total cost functions | b: sum fixed amounts and variable unit amounts; compose TK | Step 2 | 2c | 3b | 4b, 5b | Covered |
+| Calculate averages with units | c–d: totals divided by Q at two Q values | Step 3 | 2d | 3c | 5c | Covered |
+| Compare and explain within assumptions | e: compare all totals, GCK halving, GVK constant, GTK not halving | Step 4 | 2e | 3d | 4c–d, 5d | Covered |
+
+Question 6 is the target. Answer form stays a classification table with reasons, functions, two numerical rows with full units, and a bounded verbal comparison. Bloom: understand/classify, apply functions/averages, analyse totals versus averages, evaluate the halving claim. A correct number without unit or explanation is incomplete where requested.
+
+### Exercise, explanation, and worked-example sequence
+
+Fresh contexts: keychain atelier worked example; climbing-centre data retrieval; mobile podcast booth comprehension; dog-wash salon guided exercise; pottery combined-change task; birdhouse independent practice; exact bakery target; theatre-mask bonus; swimming-pool closing retrieval. The chapter's bakery continuity is reserved for its approved target. An explicit neighbor-content search found posters/bicycles in §2.1.2 and bags in §2.1.3; these draft contexts were replaced before rendering without changing operations or values. All final sources/assets use the corrected contexts.
+
+Instruction: motivating keychain atelier decision → one cost category per definition → total functions → per-product meaning → visual overview → two cost graphs and table → exact four-step worked chain. Cost formula/definition boxes and the warning about an energy bill's two components sit with the concept.
+
+Seven printed exercise headings follow the current contract. Summary is a blockquote after the worked example, not an eighth stage. Startopgaven contains prerequisite retrieval and a compact current-content check. Guided practice is an optional detour with a labelled classification table, explicit formula scaffold, then fewer prompts for averages and a bounded conclusion. Independent exercises retain any supplied classification table but remove worked hints. Pottery changes fixed rent and variable clay costs separately then together, confronting “a lower monthly bill means lower variable costs.” All support is on paper.
+
+Actual 55-minute equation: motivation 2 + instruction 11 + worked example 7 + summary/transitions 2 + Startopgaven 6 + Zelfstandige oefening 13 + Doeloefening 11 = 52 minutes. Start: Q1 3 min (read units/two rows/compare), Q2 3 min (five short checks). Independent: Q4 5 min (two changes, recombine and critique), Q5 8 min (four components, functions, six averages, explanation). Target Q6: a 2, b 2, c 2, d 2, e 3 = 11 min. Guided Q3 adds 10 minutes; teacher uses it as supported additional practice with independent work finished later, preserving all goals and target. Bonus Q7 8 minutes and closing Q8 4 minutes are outside core/homework. These are planning estimates, not observed classroom timings. Difficulty MEDIUM; estimates and ratings remain teacher-facing.
+
+### Textbook visuals and answer model
+
+Three fresh SVG/PNG pairs: fig_1 conceptual overview (totals → divide by Q → averages), fig_2 exact total-cost graph and fig_3 exact average-cost graph for the keychain atelier. Domain Q=100–200 keychains/week, TCK=120, TVK=0.50Q, TK=120+0.50Q euro/week. Average domain positive Q only. Every curve directly labelled; ceteris-paribus wording and units are adjacent. Graph geometry is checked against saved coordinates; final PNG/PDF images inspected.
+
+Answer procedure: (1) classify and explain total behaviour; (2) construct functions; (3) formula → substitution → total → average with unit; (4) compare totals, then averages, with a causal and bounded explanation. All subquestions receive a why explanation; bonus gets a model answer and criteria instead of prescribed steps. Currency averages round to two decimals.
+
+### Part A review and Part B handoff
+
+Independent reviewer: parent agent /root, separate from author assessment-paragraph. Historical review is not reused. Full new sources, figures and rendered pages require current manifest-bound review. Review is pending until recorded by that reviewer. Handoff and quality records report actual closure status. Assessment ends locally with no push, PR, deployment, merge or invented hosted CI.
